(6232502, 920055, 89468, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by citymars:</b></div><hr/><i> Good catch.  I''m not crazy about the composition, e.g., seeing the soldier''s back, but being able to see his earplug is a nice touch.  I believe the explosive fire is real (great timing, as others have said), but it sort of looks like it was added in post processing. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Oh no! I did not add it! I may have over use the recuperation tool (and the vibrance) while converting from raw, I wanted to have as much details as possible instead of a white blah. I am not quite use to it. I did not have much time to fine tune my exposition choices on the spot. Here is the original version in JPG (I shot raw + jpg).<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=921770" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89468/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_921770.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89468/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_921770.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/85000-89999/89468/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_921770.jpg"/></a> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by citymars: Good catch.  I''m not crazy about the composition, e.g., seeing the soldier''s back, but being able to see his earplug is a nice touch.  I believe the explosive fire is real (great timing, as others have said), but it sort of looks like it was added in post processing.   Oh no! I did not add it! I may have over use the recuperation tool (and the vibrance) while converting from raw, I wanted to have as much details as possible instead of a white blah. I am not quite use to it. I did not have much time to fine tune my exposition choices on the spot. Here is the original version in JPG (I shot raw + jpg).  ', '2010-11-24 18:17:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(6232510, 919818, 121082, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the advice. No on the female, must just be a girlish looking boy. Marine Corps boot camp is not co-ed, i believe the other service''s military recruit training are thou.</td>', 'Thanks for the advice. No on the female, must just be a girlish looking boy. Marine Corps boot camp is not co-ed, i believe the other service''s military recruit training are thou.', '2010-11-24 18:26:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(6232532, 919711, 94815, '<td valign="top">Congrats Lydia. I''m wondering where you got the M16. In silhouette, there is no mistaking it; so you were wise to use it well. The rest doesn''t look much like combat gear to an Army person but who cares? It''s the illusion that counts.</td>', 'Congrats Lydia. I''m wondering where you got the M16. In silhouette, there is no mistaking it; so you were wise to use it well. The rest doesn''t look much like combat gear to an Army person but who cares? It''s the illusion that counts.', '2010-11-24 18:56:02.000000', NULL, 0),
